# Craton SEO · Conversion · Market

## Conversion (do first when building)

- Replace `mailto:` with a **real form endpoint** (Formspree / Netlify Forms / webhook) + success state.
- Add **booking** path (Calendly / Cal.com) for pilots when available.
- One customer path: pilot / partner vs careers (“Join”, “Lead a product”) should not confuse buyers.
- Prefer indexable on-page product detail over content locked only in `<dialog>` / hidden tabs.

## SEO essentials

- Title ~50–60 chars, e.g. `Craton Technologies | AI for EU MDR & IVDR (RAccelerator)`.
- Keywords in H1 or first paragraph: EU MDR, IVDR, GSPR gap assessment, regulatory AI.
- Meta: description, robots, canonical, `og:*`, Twitter card, `og:image` 1200×630, favicon, apple-touch-icon.
- JSON-LD: Organization (+ logo, sameAs, contactPoint) and SoftwareApplication for products; Person for founder optional.
- Long-term: product pages + resource hub; legal routes `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/accessibility` must be real.
- Perf: trim/self-host fonts; `font-display: swap`; do not let canvas burn mobile CPU.

## Trust & market proof

- Surface strengths peers lack: patent record (link numbers when ready), founder track record, human-in-the-loop.
- Add security / data-handling section when content exists (ISO/SOC/GDPR only if true).
- Optional lead magnet later: MDR readiness checklist / one-pager (gated).
- Analytics only with consent plan (GA4 or Plausible) — ask before wiring IDs.

## Suggested build order (from review)

1. Conversion form + booking CTA  
2. Hero rewrite + SEO meta  
3. Contrast / type scale  
4. Product visuals + dual product cards  
5. Legal, analytics, security strip  
6. Split product/content pages  
